config BR2_PACKAGE_APPLE_BCE
	bool "apple-bce"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	help
	  The t2linux apple-bce kernel module for Intel Macs with the
	  Apple T2 chip (Mac mini 2018, MacBook Pro/Air 2018-2020,
	  iMac 2020, iMac Pro, Mac Pro 2019): the T2's internal USB
	  devices (VHCI) and its sound card "Apple T2 Audio" (built-in
	  speaker, headphone jack). Selected by the IYAKKI "mac" variant
	  only (configs/iyakki_mac.fragment). Out of tree, GPL-2.0,
	  built against the image's own kernel.

	  https://github.com/t2linux/apple-bce-drv

comment "apple-bce needs a Linux kernel to be built (x86_64)"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
